 Long term necessity:
 
 - Figure out how to properly id downloaded games and resources from arbitrary creators
     - I would prefer a completely decentralized system even if it leads to occasional id conflicts, but they should be very rare
	 - Maybe creators can generate a uniqueID and the game can use that to keep track of ids for games/images etc
	     - So the game can come up with locally unique id numbers for each asset
		    Based on a sort of creator-local asset id (first image I upload is image 0)
			Games can reference their own creators asset by creator local id, or define other creators by uniqueID and reference their assets by creator+creator-local id
			then the engine translates that to the number it uses to keep track of stuff it has (engine id)
	- Tile and Entity IDs should just be game-local and shouldn't need any of that

- Set up a home server (Maker style but the games themselves, not just levels)
    - interface so you can upload games/levels/assets to, explore and download them too
	- server needs to at the very least be configurable so it could be pointed somewhere else easily for custom stuff or if I eventually abandon hosting it

- Managed server system to take uploads, allow downloading games, allow uploading levelpacks/mods of games
    - I'm going to have to figure out moderation, no way around it
	- Probably need good secure authentication too
	- This might end up needing to be a paid thing who knows
	    - I hope all engine features can still be usable with no server, no account etc
 
